// process-compute.config — used directly as nextflow.config by Cirro
// (per Day 2 research). Single-process resource allocation since Q10
// chose the black-box wrapping option — one process gets one resource
// allocation for the entire pipeline run (tif_conversion through
// survival), which is the known tradeoff of that choice vs. five staged,
// independently-sized processes.
//
// PLACEHOLDER VALUES — not tuned against a real CRC TMA run's actual
// peak memory/CPU. Needs a real run's numbers before trusting this for
// production AWS Batch billing/sizing.

// FIX 2026-09-30: main.nf's process block declares its OWN inline `container
// params.container` directive (not just relying on this file's `process.container`
// below) -- and main.nf ALSO used to unconditionally overwrite params.container
// with "spatia-pipeline:latest" as its very first line, every single run,
// regardless of what this file or process-input.json supplied. That stomped
// this file's container pin completely: the last real run
// (2026-09-30, PW_DATASET=6c59b585) tried to pull "spatia-pipeline:latest" --
// an image that was never pushed anywhere Batch can reach -- instead of the
// real ghcr.io image below, and failed with CannotPullImageManifestError.
// main.nf's default is now guarded (params.container = params.container ?: ...),
// so this params.container line is what actually reaches the process.
// process.container below is kept too, redundant but harmless, in case a
// future edit removes main.nf's inline container directive.
params.container = 'ghcr.io/afroozjahedi/spatia-pipeline:latest'


// SWITCHED TO :latest 2026-09-30 -- the previously-pinned SHA tag
// (2db742a...) was built from a Dockerfile with a broken ENTRYPOINT (see
// that fix's commit). :latest is what build-spatia-image.yml pushes on
// every manual workflow run, alongside a SHA tag -- using :latest avoids
// a manual re-pin after every rebuild during the Summit crunch. TRADEOFF,
// flagged not hidden: :latest is mutable, so a run's actual image can
// change without a corresponding git commit here -- fine for active
// debugging, but re-pin to an immutable digest/SHA once this stabilizes,
// especially before anything that needs to be reproducible for the paper.
process {
    container = 'ghcr.io/afroozjahedi/spatia-pipeline:latest'
    cpus   = 8
    memory = '256 GB'
    time   = '12h'
    // ADDED 2026-10-30: run cirro-d361f-f3b76 died at image 40/130 with
    // "Host EC2 instance terminated" (AWS reclaimed the machine -- most likely a
    // Spot interruption, not a code error). Because the whole pipeline is ONE
    // process, any lost machine loses the entire run. Retry ONLY on
    // infrastructure-type exits (unknown exit / killed), never on real Python
    // errors, so a genuine bug still fails fast instead of burning 3x compute.
    errorStrategy = { (task.exitStatus == null || task.exitStatus == Integer.MAX_VALUE
                       || task.exitStatus in [137, 143]) ? 'retry' : 'terminate' }
    maxRetries    = 2
}

aws {
    batch {
        // ADDED 2026-10-30: let AWS Batch itself re-launch the job if a Spot
        // instance is reclaimed (Nextflow's default is 0 = no Spot retries).
        maxSpotAttempts = 3
        // Confirmed with Dima (2026-09-25): Cirro assigns the queue/compute
        // environment itself at submission time — nothing to hardcode here.
    }
}
